<task id="011" project="messaging-communication-app-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>BFF filtered communication query endpoint (thread/regarding/channel/date facets; participant= stubbed until W5 per FR-02)</title>
    <phase>W1 — BFF Reads (CC-3)</phase>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <estimated-hours>6</estimated-hours>
    <deps>002</deps>
    <blocks>051,080</blocks>
    <tags>bff-api, communication</tags>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Adds a NEW filtered read endpoint to `Sprk.Bff.Api` that backs the global grid + workspace widget queries and MUST enforce NFR-03 access parity (impersonation + 2-rule filter) on every facet — no message content may bypass the BFF filter. BFF-touching: publish-size + CVE + bff-extensions Placement Justification required; access-filter no-leak correctness demands code-review + adr-check at Step 9.5. Modifies `.cs` in shared `Services/Communication/` (additive).</rigor-reason>
    <parallel-group>W1</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <fr-refs>FR-02, NFR-03</fr-refs>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <effort>high</effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Add a single new filtered-query route to the EXISTING communication endpoint group and the supporting query method to the EXISTING read service:

    • **Route** — `GET /api/communications?thread=&regarding=&channel=&from=&to=` on `src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/CommunicationEndpoints.cs` (add to the existing `MapGroup("/api/communications")` — NO new endpoint group).
    • **Service support** — a filtered-query method on `src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/CommunicationThreadReadService.cs` that composes the query facets onto the SAME impersonation read path used by task 010.

    Returns a filtered communication list in the R1 DTO shape (reuse `CommunicationThreadReadModels.cs`). The **thread / regarding / channel / date facets** all reuse the read path (`IImpersonatedCommunicationQuery`) + the access filter (`Access/CommunicationAccessFilter.cs`):
    - `thread=` → filter `sprk_communication` by `sprk_thread`
    - `regarding=` → resolve via `RegardingFieldMap` (entity-set-agnostic, same resolution task 010 uses)
    - `channel=` → filter by `sprk_communicationtype`
    - `from=` / `to=` → date-range filter by `sprk_sentat`

    **`participant=` is STUBBED in this task** — it is wired in **task 051** after the `sprk_communicationparticipant` junction (003) + participant-index write (050) land. In task 011, `participant=` MUST be **inert / graceful**: either reject it with an ADR-019 ProblemDetails "not-yet-supported" response OR ignore it (documented), and NEVER attempt a text-LIKE fallback over the `;`-joined address text. State this explicitly in code + PR. Blocks 051.

    **NFR-03 access parity is the load-bearing correctness property.** Every facet routes through `IImpersonatedCommunicationQuery` + `CommunicationAccessFilter` (impersonation + 2-rule privacy + internal-only). Do **NOT** author a new access mechanism, a bespoke ACL, or reintroduce **membership-union on reads** (retired 2026-07-16). Unknown / empty / malformed filters degrade gracefully (no 500 — empty result or ADR-019 bad-request as appropriate).
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Spaarke BFF engineer for the Communication subsystem. Authority on `src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/CommunicationEndpoints.cs` + `Services/Communication/` reads. Fluent in ADR-028 (blessed impersonation read path), ADR-008 (endpoint filters), ADR-019 (ProblemDetails — graceful degradation), ADR-024 (11-entity regarding family / `RegardingFieldMap`), the R1 impersonation + 2-rule access model, NFR-03 access parity, §10 BFF Hygiene, and §11 Component Justification.
  </role>

  <goal>
    A `GET /api/communications?thread=&regarding=&channel=&from=&to=` filtered-query endpoint exists on the existing communication group, backed by a filtered-query method on `CommunicationThreadReadService`, returning access-filtered communications in the R1 DTO shape. thread/regarding/channel/date facets reuse the impersonation read path + `CommunicationAccessFilter`; `participant=` is stubbed (inert/graceful, wired in 051). Every facet honors NFR-03 (impersonation + 2-rule; no new mechanism, no membership-union); unknown/empty filters degrade gracefully. The endpoint carries the ADR-008 authorization filter + ADR-019 ProblemDetails and is registered unconditionally. Build clean; per-facet + access-filter tests pass; publish-size delta + CVE + bff-extensions Placement Justification reported.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      The global All-Communications grid (Surface 2, task 040/041) and the rich workspace widget (Surface 3, task 030) present communications filtered by channel / person / date / regarding across records. While those UI surfaces read the DataGrid via `Xrm.WebApi`, the filtered `query` endpoint is the BFF-mediated equivalent that honors the `internal-only` access rule the client-fetch path cannot enforce — and it is the endpoint task 051 completes with the `participant=` facet once the junction lands. Today the communication read surface is thread-id-scoped only (`CommunicationEndpoints.cs`); there is no cross-record filtered query.

      Component Justification (§11): (1) **Existing** — grep-verified: `CommunicationEndpoints.cs` is thread-id-scoped; no route filters communications by channel/person/date/regarding across records. But `CommunicationThreadReadService` + `IImpersonatedCommunicationQuery` + `CommunicationAccessFilter` + `RegardingFieldMap` already own the read + filter + regarding map. (2) **Extension** — ONE additive route + ONE additive query method reusing all existing pieces; no new service, no new access mechanism, no second filter. (3) **Cost-of-doing-nothing (concrete)** — without the filtered `query` endpoint the global grid / widget cannot filter by person/channel/date across records through the access-honoring BFF path, and there is no endpoint for task 051 to complete with `participant=` (FR-02 acceptance fails); if any facet bypassed the access filter, private/internal-only content would leak (NFR-03 security failure). Named contract failures, not "future flexibility."

      Why `participant=` is stubbed here: the exact person facet requires the `sprk_communicationparticipant` junction (task 003 schema) + the participant-index write (task 050) — neither exists in W1. A text-LIKE fallback over the `;`-joined `sprk_from/to/cc` text would return wrong results with no role precision and is explicitly forbidden (spec §11). So `participant=` is inert/graceful in W1 and wired in W5 (task 051). This task BLOCKS 051 (the facet has nowhere to land without the route) and 080 (seam tests).

      NFR-03 access parity (binding): every facet MUST apply R1's impersonation + 2-rule filter and MUST NOT reintroduce membership-union on reads (retired 2026-07-16). Graceful degradation: unknown/empty/malformed filters yield an empty result or an ADR-019 bad-request — never a 500 and never an unfiltered dump.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/CommunicationEndpoints.cs (ADD the filtered `query` route to the existing `/api/communications` group)</file>
