  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Read `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md` §F/§G + §11 Component Justification + `docs/standards/DATA-ACCESS-DECISION-CRITERIA.md` + `../messaging-communication-app-r1/notes/access-model-decision.md` (no membership-union) before adding the endpoint.</step>
    <step order="2">Read `CommunicationThreadReadService.cs`, `IImpersonatedCommunicationQuery.cs`, `CommunicationAccessFilter.cs`, `CommunicationThreadReadModels.cs`, and `RegardingFieldMap.cs` to identify the impersonation-query entry point + access-filter call + DTO shape to reuse, and the `sprk_thread` / `sprk_communicationtype` / `sprk_sentat` column names for the facets. Coordinate with task 010 (same read path) to avoid divergent method shapes.</step>
    <step order="3">Grep `CommunicationEndpoints.cs` + the read service to confirm no cross-record filtered `query` route exists (§11 existing-question evidence).</step>
    <step order="4">Implement the filtered-query method on `CommunicationThreadReadService`: compose an OData filter from `thread` (`sprk_thread`), `regarding` (via `RegardingFieldMap`, entity-set-agnostic), `channel` (`sprk_communicationtype`), `from`/`to` (`sprk_sentat` range) → run through `IImpersonatedCommunicationQuery` → compose privacy + internal-only via `CommunicationAccessFilter` → project into the R1 DTO shape. No new filter, no membership-union, no text-LIKE participant fallback.</step>
    <step order="5">Add the `participant=` STUB: accept the param in the route contract but return an ADR-019 not-yet-supported ProblemDetails (or documented inert behavior); add a code comment + PR note that task 051 wires it against the `sprk_communicationparticipant` junction. Never text-LIKE over `;`-joined address text.</step>
    <step order="6">Add `GET /api/communications?thread=&regarding=&channel=&from=&to=&participant=` to the existing `/api/communications` group in `CommunicationEndpoints.cs`: bind query params, call the filtered-query method, apply the ADR-008 authorization filter + ADR-019 ProblemDetails (graceful on bad/unknown/empty filters); register unconditionally (ADR-032/ADR-010).</step>
    <step order="7">Write tests in `tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/`: (a) per-facet coverage — `thread=`, `regarding=` (entity-set-agnostic), `channel=`, `from`/`to` each filter correctly; (b) the access filter is applied on the filtered path (NEGATIVE — a private/internal-only message the caller may not see is absent from a facet result); (c) graceful degradation — unknown/empty/malformed filter yields empty/ADR-019, not 500; (d) `participant=` returns the not-yet-supported/inert response and does NOT text-LIKE; (e) no second filter / no membership-union reintroduced (grep/diff-verifiable).</step>
    <step order="8">Run `dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/` + `dotnet test tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/ --filter Communication`; confirm existing communication tests still pass.</step>
    <step order="9.1">Run `dotnet publish -c Release src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/ -o deploy/api-publish/`; report compressed size + delta vs ~46.99 MB baseline. Expected ≈ 0 (no new packages).</step>
    <step order="9.2">Run `dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive` — confirm no new HIGH-severity CVEs.</step>
    <step order="9.5">FULL-rigor quality gates: `code-review` on the diff (focus per-facet access-filter application / no-leak / no membership-union / participant stub is genuinely inert); `adr-check` against `spec.md` (focus FR-02/NFR-03, ADR-028 read-path reuse, ADR-008/019/024, §11 justification). Address Critical findings; cite bff-extensions Placement Justification.</step>
    <step order="10">Run `/conflict-check` before the PR (BFF hot-path; shared `Services/Communication/`; coordinate with task 010 on the same read path + `spaarke-notification-spine-r1`).</step>
    <step order="11">Update `tasks/TASK-INDEX.md` (011 ✅) + `current-task.md`; record decisions (facet→column map, participant-stub contract for 051, access-filter reuse point, graceful-degradation policy).</step>
  </steps>

