  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">`GET /api/communications?thread=&regarding=&channel=&from=&to=` exists on the existing `/api/communications` group and returns a filtered communication list in the R1 DTO shape (reuses `CommunicationThreadReadModels`).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Each of thread / regarding / channel / date facets filters correctly and is covered by a test; `regarding=` resolves entity-set-agnostically via `RegardingFieldMap`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Every facet routes through `IImpersonatedCommunicationQuery` + `CommunicationAccessFilter` — no new access mechanism, no second/divergent filter, and NO membership-union is reintroduced (grep/diff-verifiable).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">NEGATIVE: a private/internal-only message the caller may not see is absent from a facet result (access filter applied on the filtered path).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Graceful degradation: an unknown / empty / malformed filter yields an empty result or an ADR-019 ProblemDetails bad-request — never a 500 and never an unfiltered dump.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`participant=` is inert/graceful (ADR-019 not-yet-supported or documented no-op), does NOT perform a text-LIKE fallback, and leaves a defined seam for task 051.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The route carries the ADR-008 authorization filter + ADR-019 ProblemDetails and is registered unconditionally (ADR-032).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`dotnet build` clean; existing communication tests still pass; publish-size delta ≈ 0 vs ~46.99 MB; no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    Depends on 002 (thread typed-regarding lookups + Lookup discriminator — the `regarding=` facet reads over them). Blocks 051 (the `participant=` facet completion) and 080 (per-facet + access-parity seam tests). Shares the impersonation read path with task 010 — coordinate on the read-service method shape so 010 and 011 do not diverge (both are W1, parallel-safe, but touch the same file additively; `/conflict-check` before PR). The single most important correctness property is no-leak on every facet: the negative access case is non-negotiable (NFR-03, security-sensitive). The `participant=` text-LIKE fallback is explicitly forbidden (spec §11) — leave it inert until the junction lands.
  </notes>

